From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:34:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gfx: JIHAD_GPU_NPIXMAP_TILES=1 uploads tiles through Palm
 native pixmaps (T-636)

gpu-bench section 20 found Palm's libnapp NPixmap, bound as an EGLImage texture
(EGL_NATIVE_PIXMAP_KHR, as Palm's NRemoteTexture does), samples CPU writes live.

With the switch on, BasicTextureImage::DirectUpdate copies a tile's rows into a pooled
NPixmapPrivate and binds its texture instead of glTexImage2D/glTexSubImage2D:
- BGRA memory samples as RGBA, the same formats a GL_BGRA upload leaves.
- The first write after a sync waits on an EGL_KHR_fence_sync fence.
- Pinned memory is capped at JIHAD_GPU_NPIXMAP_MB (48).
- Any load or create failure falls back to GL uploads for the process, with one line.
'upload totals' lines compare both paths. Unset: GL uploads as before, plus a counter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MpagfP34fXBdsc76E8YSzR
